  "comparison_notes": [
    "Expected values authored before extraction; source spans and trigger prose are evidence, not exact-match keys.",
    "Band deadline is the IR-level encoding of 'whichever comes first' (10 business days, 20th of next month) as the policy.py `earliest` kind.",
    "Field names in the supplied OpenAPI are abbreviated (cust_ref, item_id, sum, amt_due, dl_days, tilgung_min, kk_min, l_min, h_min); the compiler maps them onto the IR's semantic slots via the existing needles.",
    "Identity field names (kontonummer, gruendungsdatum, plz) are German abbreviations; the verify_identity `field` enum lists them verbatim.",
    "Outcome table comparison is order-insensitive; identity and attempt order are significant.",
    "Calendar holidays are deliberately short (two year-end dates); any hidden brief with no holidays should set calendar.holidays = []."
  ]
